  "content": {
    "id": "p34-q77-node",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "77",
    "prompt": "The derivative of $y=x^m\\sqrt{a+bx^2}$ is in the form\n$$y'=\\frac{x^{m-1}}{\\sqrt{a+bx^2}}h(x)$$\nfor some function $h$. Find $h(x)$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$h(x)=ma+b(m+1)x^2$.\n\nUse the product rule and combine terms over $\\sqrt{a+bx^2}$.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}y'&=mx^{m-1}\\sqrt{a+bx^2}+\\frac{bx^{m+1}}{\\sqrt{a+bx^2}}\\\\y'&=\\frac{x^{m-1}}{\\sqrt{a+bx^2}}\\bigl[m(a+bx^2)+bx^2\\bigr]\\\\y'&=\\frac{x^{m-1}}{\\sqrt{a+bx^2}}\\bigl[ma+b(m+1)x^2\\bigr]\\end{align*}$$\nHence $h(x)=ma+b(m+1)x^2$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 38
  },
